export anchor SewingPatternStyle:
    number: 110
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Sewing pattern
    idea: Every panel is a numbered pattern piece on tissue paper, with a dashed cutting line, an inner stitching line, notches and grain arrows, and progress drawn as a grain arrow sewn part way.
    base: light
    palette:
        tissue: #f3e9d2, the page, with faint crinkle lines and pale highlights
        lightTissue: #f8f1e0, piece fills, the search and the instruction sheet
        printBlack: #1d1b17, text, cut and stitch lines, notches and the primary button
        patternBlue: #1f4e8c, grain arrows, progress, this week bars, piece letters and focus
        markingRed: #a12a2a, the overdue mark, Behind and the count badge
        green: #2f6233, On track
        amber: #7d4e00, At risk
        tapeYellow: #f2d04a, the tape measure axis with dark text
        pencil: #5b5345, meta and times
    type:
        Two stacks. Labels and titles use Franklin Gothic Medium, Franklin
        Gothic, ITC Franklin Gothic, Arial at regular weight. Text uses
        Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans, Tahoma. The greeting is 40px at 1.08,
        measurements 52px, piece titles 19px, piece letters 30px blue,
        labels 12 to 14px caps tracked 0.14 to 0.18em, body 14px at 1.6.
    layout:
        A pattern envelope header shows a pattern piece logo, Brightwork
        with Pattern no. 1031, a boxed search, a black New project button,
        a round bell and a round MO, over a solid rule. The nav is caps, the
        current item blue with a small triangle notch. The board is a 12
        column cutting table of pieces, each with a 2px dashed cut line, a
        1px solid stitch line 12px inside, black triangle notches on edges,
        scissors on the top cut line and a circled piece number with a caps
        note like Front Cut 1. Piece 1 has a big curved bottom right corner
        and holds Good morning, Mara, the date, a red underlined 4 tasks are
        overdue with a crossed circle and a grain arrow. Piece 2 holds
        Finished measurements, four numbers each over a blue dimension line.
        Piece 3 is the cutting layout, six smaller pieces lettered A to F
        three across, some with one curved corner, each with name, meta, a
        grain arrow solid to the percent and dashed after, the percent and
        status. Piece 4 is the chart with dashed outline hatched bars for
        last week and solid blue bars for this week standing on a yellow
        tape measure marked 18 to 31. Piece 5 is Sewing steps, six activity
        items with circled numbers. Below 1000px pieces go full width.
    spacing: An 8px unit. A 12px seam allowance between the cut line and the stitch line, 28px between pieces.
    density: Medium. Pieces of different sizes laid out on a 12 column cutting table.
    corners: Square, with one big curved corner on some pieces, like an armhole or hem curve.
    borders: 2px dashed outer cut line, 1px solid inner stitch line and black triangle notches on edges.
    shadows: None. Tissue lies flat.
    icons:
        Pattern markings at 16px. A filled dot for On track, a filled
        triangle for At risk, a square inside a square for Behind and a
        crossed circle for overdue, with the caps word. Line scissors sit on
        every cut line.
    focus: A 2px blue outline offset 3px with a soft 6px blue tint around it.
    tone: Pattern instructions, such as Cut 1, Finished measurements and Sewing steps.
